title: Unify ownership checking into one flow-sensitive analysis
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: high
blocked_by: ['8-5']
created_at: '2026-07-29T00:00:00'
updated_at: '2026-07-30T00:00:00'
description: 'Review item 16. Replace the two overlapping half-checkers with one analysis.
  src/ownership/ sees everything but is the weaker: flow-insensitive across branches (a
  move in ''then'' mutates outer VarState in place via lookup_mut,
  src/ownership/mod.rs:123-130, no snapshot/merge at verify.rs:58-68), single-pass on
  loops with no fixpoint (verify.rs:69-95), borrow counts that increment and never
  release (mod.rs:148-183), call arguments never treated as moves (verify.rs:233-241).
  The typer has correct snapshot/restore and branch-union merge
  (src/typer/mod.rs:488-514) plus a loop re-move check but only for explicit take. Build
  on the typer''s machinery: branch snapshot and union merge, loop fixpoint, scoped
  borrow release, calls as moves-or-borrows per D1. DoD: the analysis is the single
  authority and the redundant path is deleted not disabled; section 3.3 rejected with
  the D1 diagnostic; the tests/audit_alpha/negative_* corpus still passes; jinn check
  runs it so check and build agree (check currently skips ownership entirely,
  src/driver/mod.rs:249-280, and passes a heap-corrupting program); unify the two driver
  pipelines so jinn build stops skipping HirValidator (driver/pipeline.rs omits it,
  driver/mod.rs:437 runs it).'
